we just gotta send one
person to Joshua Tree,

00:36:03.570 --> 00:36:07.300
have them do everything,
while wearing the interface

00:36:07.300 --> 00:36:11.060
and then if I can have
the exact same experience,

00:36:11.060 --> 00:36:13.020
why am I gonna get in the car and drive?

00:36:13.020 --> 00:36:16.434
Yeah that's convenient,
but I'm just sayin'.

00:36:16.434 --> 00:36:17.267
You're provin' my point.

00:36:17.267 --> 00:36:19.810
That doesn't seem healthy
either, specifically.

00:36:19.810 --> 00:36:20.693
So in general this whole thing--

00:36:20.693 --> 00:36:23.040
I don't think we're ever
gonna get to that point.

00:36:23.040 --> 00:36:25.890
Even with technology and
the way that it's advancing,

00:36:25.890 --> 00:36:28.400
I think there's just too
many limitations, okay.

00:36:28.400 --> 00:36:30.880
But if we reel it back to today,

00:36:30.880 --> 00:36:31.870
I'll try to make it simple.

00:36:31.870 --> 00:36:34.970
Because I think I'm adopting a practice

00:36:34.970 --> 00:36:37.260
that is my answer to this.

00:36:37.260 --> 00:36:40.533
I've never articulated it,
so as I try to do that,

00:36:41.700 --> 00:36:43.063
let's see if it holds up.

00:36:45.020 --> 00:36:47.560
I think there's a balance
between, you know,

00:36:47.560 --> 00:36:49.500
this is kind of a middle
of the road thing.

00:36:49.500 --> 00:36:50.690
Which may seem obvious.

00:36:50.690 --> 00:36:52.560
But there's a balance between
not taking any photos,

00:36:52.560 --> 00:36:53.530
takin' too many photos.

00:36:53.530 --> 00:36:56.210
So I think the goal is to know,

00:36:56.210 --> 00:36:58.790
how to take just the
right amount of photos.

00:36:58.790 --> 00:36:59.940
And I'll be more specific.

00:36:59.940 --> 00:37:02.280
I think if there's any moment,

00:37:02.280 --> 00:37:05.630
and I believe that I try to make my goal,

00:37:05.630 --> 00:37:08.100
especially when I've made
plans to do somethin'

00:37:08.100 --> 00:37:10.750
that's event-based, well when I'm in it,

00:37:10.750 --> 00:37:12.850
I really want to appreciate it.

00:37:12.850 --> 00:37:16.763
To be in that moment and
savor it for all that it is.

00:37:17.870 --> 00:37:20.720
And then I've noticed that if I do that,

00:37:20.720 --> 00:37:22.340
if recall that intention

00:37:23.780 --> 00:37:26.793
and I start to really
appreciate the moment,

00:37:27.630 --> 00:37:32.630
that then if I add a little
brain trigger to that conclusion

00:37:34.980 --> 00:37:36.880
that oh yeah I am in the moment,

00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:40.670
that like at some point
around here in time,

00:37:40.670 --> 00:37:43.780
I'm gonna snap a photo, in
order to help me remember

00:37:43.780 --> 00:37:44.910
a moment when I was in the moment.

00:37:44.910 --> 00:37:45.860
Now I don't wanna--

00:37:45.860 --> 00:37:47.790
It's actually almost a way
to signify that this moment

00:37:47.790 --> 00:37:49.500
is worth being in.

00:37:49.500 --> 00:37:52.530
Yeah, but not dropping what I'm doing

00:37:52.530 --> 00:37:55.000
in order to get the perfect
frame, or something right now.

00:37:55.000 --> 00:37:56.820
But just sayin', I'm makin' a mental note,

00:37:56.820 --> 00:37:58.900
that like at the right time,

00:37:58.900 --> 00:38:02.970
maybe when the height of
this moment has passed,

00:38:02.970 --> 00:38:05.680
I will snap a picture to commemorate it.

00:38:05.680 --> 00:38:10.240
Or, if I can snap a photo
and put my phone back away

00:38:10.240 --> 00:38:12.250
and still be in the
moment, I'm gonna do that.

00:38:12.250 --> 00:38:14.230
As opposed to making the moment,

00:38:14.230 --> 00:38:15.770
tryin' to capture the moment.

00:38:15.770 --> 00:38:18.800
Which incidentally, I'm
sure you've seen this,

00:38:18.800 --> 00:38:23.093
but if you live in Los Angeles
and you go to any place,

00:38:24.751 --> 00:38:27.763
you will see, it's usually a couple,

00:38:28.700 --> 00:38:30.773
and it's usually,

00:38:33.750 --> 00:38:36.100
this is definitely a
generalization, so lemme just say,

00:38:36.100 --> 00:38:39.862
in my experience, eight outta
10 times, there is a woman,

00:38:39.862 --> 00:38:44.862
who is on the attractive side,
and she is doing something,

00:38:44.890 --> 00:38:47.920
and her boyfriend or husband has a camera

00:38:47.920 --> 00:38:49.530
and is being forced to sit there

00:38:49.530 --> 00:38:52.407
and take 100 pictures
of her doing something,

00:38:52.407 --> 00:38:53.930
No, no, no,
for her Instagram.

00:38:53.930 --> 00:38:58.930
he forces her, she forces
him to take a photo, or five.

00:38:59.810 --> 00:39:01.850
Then she comes and looks
at 'em, gives notes--

00:39:01.850 --> 00:39:03.870
And then she goes back to where she was.

00:39:03.870 --> 00:39:05.880
That happens five more times.

00:39:05.880 --> 00:39:09.710
And this is, okay, I think
we are both in agreement,

00:39:09.710 --> 00:39:12.640
that this is way outta bounds.

00:39:12.640 --> 00:39:15.130
I understand that maybe
Instagramming is your career,

00:39:15.130 --> 00:39:16.633
but what I, good luck.

00:39:18.070 --> 00:39:18.940
That doesn't apply.

00:39:18.940 --> 00:39:21.723
Yeah if you're a model
or an Instagram person--

00:39:21.723 --> 00:39:25.740
That is outside of the realm
of being in the moment.

00:39:25.740 --> 00:39:30.560
Because the moment has become
about you getting the moment,

00:39:30.560 --> 00:39:35.110
not for yourself, but
for accolades, admiration

00:39:35.110 --> 00:39:36.350
that you're gonna get on Instagram.

00:39:36.350 --> 00:39:38.030
Now, 'cause I don't
know that you did this,

00:39:38.030 --> 00:39:41.210
but if you're doin' this
meditation on the rocks,

00:39:41.210 --> 00:39:43.460
and it's like wow, this
is an amazing moment.

00:39:44.330 --> 00:39:46.340
The way that I'm saying you would do that

00:39:46.340 --> 00:39:47.870
is you would just pull out a phone,

00:39:47.870 --> 00:39:49.160
I'd look outta the corner of my eye,

00:39:49.160 --> 00:39:52.070
I'd see my son over there
on a meditation rock,

00:39:52.070 --> 00:39:56.003
I'd pull out my phone,
I'd take a snapshot.

00:39:57.270 --> 00:39:59.560
And then I'd put it back
away and I'd keep meditating.

00:39:59.560 --> 00:40:00.683
It wouldn't become like,

00:40:00.683 --> 00:40:03.740
lemme figure out how to
take the next 20 minutes

00:40:03.740 --> 00:40:05.480
to make this Instagram pose.
In that moment,

00:40:05.480 --> 00:40:07.070
that's exactly what I did.

00:40:07.070 --> 00:40:10.360
There were a coupla other
moments where we were hiking

00:40:10.360 --> 00:40:14.690
and we hiked into this
cave, and then we realized

00:40:14.690 --> 00:40:19.673
that there was a really
cool opening into the sky.

00:40:20.650 --> 00:40:23.810
And we took, I'd say we stopped

00:40:23.810 --> 00:40:28.810
and we took like two minutes
getting Shepherd like set up

00:40:28.870 --> 00:40:31.740
in this cave to like take this picture.

00:40:31.740 --> 00:40:34.590
But it wasn't like this
everything is stopping

00:40:34.590 --> 00:40:35.730
for an extended period of time.

00:40:35.730 --> 00:40:37.763
It was like, oh this is a cool photo op.

00:40:39.160 --> 00:40:41.493
Let's capture this moment
in a stylistic way.

00:40:42.850 --> 00:40:45.490
All that to say, the way
that I did it last time,

00:40:45.490 --> 00:40:50.280
I do not feel like I ever
made it about the photos

00:40:50.280 --> 00:40:53.720
to the extent that I lost the
ability to be in the moment.

00:40:53.720 --> 00:40:57.280
I feel like I was in what I
would say is my sweet spot,

00:40:57.280 --> 00:40:59.810
which is what I planned to do.

00:40:59.810 --> 00:41:03.110
But I do think, that there are times,

00:41:03.110 --> 00:41:04.270
when a conscious choice

00:41:04.270 --> 00:41:06.620
to be like, I'm not gonna take any photos.

00:41:06.620 --> 00:41:09.820
Maybe when you're by yourself.

00:41:09.820 --> 00:41:12.810
Like I know we both talked
about potentially doing,

00:41:12.810 --> 00:41:17.056
and my therapist has been
pushing me to do this for awhile,

00:41:17.056 --> 00:41:19.610
take a solo trip somewhere.

00:41:19.610 --> 00:41:22.020
I've done it a coupla times or whatever.

00:41:22.020 --> 00:41:24.420
I feel like if I were to
do something like that,

00:41:26.940 --> 00:41:28.410
having an extended period
of time where I was like,

00:41:28.410 --> 00:41:29.710
I'm not takin' any photos.

00:41:29.710 --> 00:41:32.890
No, I'm sayin' everything
that's worth doing,

00:41:32.890 --> 00:41:34.600
that's worth experiencing,

00:41:34.600 --> 00:41:37.050
if you find yourself
truly experiencing it,

00:41:37.050 --> 00:41:38.330
you're in the moment,

00:41:38.330 --> 00:41:40.700
that then you should find the right way

00:41:40.700 --> 00:41:43.860
to as quickly as
possible, take a snapshot,

00:41:43.860 --> 00:41:46.270
which will help solidify it.

00:41:46.270 --> 00:41:49.207
So it's not just a, you
wanna take a mental picture--

00:41:51.876 --> 00:41:53.620
But what if you wanna,

00:41:53.620 --> 00:41:55.110
I think that's a fine general practice.

00:41:55.110 --> 00:41:57.060
So here's what I'm thinkin', so like,

00:41:57.980 --> 00:42:00.090
whenever I'm doing somethin',
like if I go campin',

00:42:00.090 --> 00:42:01.730
I'm like, you know what,
I wanna take a picture

00:42:01.730 --> 00:42:05.160
that like helps me
remember this whole thing.

00:42:05.160 --> 00:42:06.870
And then I don't wanna
keep takin' pictures.

00:42:06.870 --> 00:42:09.776
So once we set up camp,
I'm gonna walk over here

00:42:09.776 --> 00:42:12.270
and I'm gonna take a big
picture of the campsite,

00:42:12.270 --> 00:42:14.573
with as many people as
I'm campin' with in it.

00:42:16.140 --> 00:42:17.813
That's just for me if
I look back through it.

00:42:17.813 --> 00:42:19.780
I say, oh yeah, I remember that campsite,

00:42:19.780 --> 00:42:21.080
I remember this whole weekend.

00:42:21.080 --> 00:42:22.610
And then if there's a moment within that,

00:42:22.610 --> 00:42:24.330
like oh we found this waterfall,

00:42:24.330 --> 00:42:25.730
or like we're sittin' around the campfire

00:42:25.730 --> 00:42:28.720
and we're havin' this conversation.

00:42:28.720 --> 00:42:30.800
I'm gonna pull out my phone,

00:42:30.800 --> 00:42:32.330
and I'm gonna take like one picture

00:42:32.330 --> 00:42:35.303
and then I'll be like,
you know what, I got it.

00:42:36.780 --> 00:42:38.530
Any of that memory that might be lost

00:42:38.530 --> 00:42:42.210
from not having a picture,
I've now mitigated that risk

00:42:42.210 --> 00:42:44.860
and I can be back in the
moment, and then I put it away.

00:42:44.860 --> 00:42:48.800
Now I think adding the factor

00:42:48.800 --> 00:42:52.520
of trying to put it on the internet,

00:42:52.520 --> 00:42:56.510
severely complicates
things, for me personally.

00:42:56.510 --> 00:42:57.990
But you don't make that decision,

00:42:57.990 --> 00:42:59.035
you don't make that decision

00:42:59.035 --> 00:42:59.868
in the moment.
Yes you do,

00:42:59.868 --> 00:43:02.870
because it's the difference
between takin' a photo

00:43:02.870 --> 00:43:05.110
to capture a moment for you,

00:43:05.110 --> 00:43:07.200
and capturing somethin' that looks good

00:43:07.200 --> 00:43:09.745
that people will like on the internet.

00:43:09.745 --> 00:43:11.590
I don't think that
there's, I don't think that

00:43:11.590 --> 00:43:13.348
that's a super
Composition.

00:43:13.348 --> 00:43:14.820
I don't think there's a huge delineation

00:43:14.820 --> 00:43:16.610
between those two.
Posing.

00:43:16.610 --> 00:43:20.693
I think for most people,

00:43:22.400 --> 00:43:24.940
this might be because
you're such a perfectionist,

00:43:24.940 --> 00:43:26.650
and if you're gonna take somethin'

00:43:26.650 --> 00:43:29.380
for the purpose of display,

00:43:29.380 --> 00:43:31.370
you get too in your head about
it and take too much time

00:43:31.370 --> 00:43:32.370
to make it right.
It's like that woman

00:43:32.370 --> 00:43:34.700
who's makin' sure you
get it, she wants to look

00:43:34.700 --> 00:43:35.767
exactly like she wants to look, you know.

00:43:35.767 --> 00:43:37.470
But if you feel like,

00:43:37.470 --> 00:43:39.810
like I honestly don't go to that place.

00:43:39.810 --> 00:43:42.770
Just like I'm, okay I wanna
take a picture of this.

00:43:42.770 --> 00:43:44.110
Am I in exactly the right place

00:43:44.110 --> 00:43:46.380
to take the best picture
of that, probably not.

00:43:46.380 --> 00:43:48.140
But I'm not gonna take the
time to figure that out.

00:43:48.140 --> 00:43:49.200
It's just when I frame it,

00:43:49.200 --> 00:43:50.580
I'll think about the rule of thirds

00:43:50.580 --> 00:43:53.733
and I'll take visually pleasing shot.

00:43:54.930 --> 00:43:57.140
And then I'll go back,
when I get back home,

00:43:57.140 --> 00:43:59.810
and I'm like showin' Jessie,
hey here's what we did,

00:43:59.810 --> 00:44:03.630
here's the pictures, so she
can kinda live vicariously

00:44:03.630 --> 00:44:06.110
